  "design_notes": "Tiny is one bread-bin cube of a head with floating block hands and flat square feet, so in silhouette it is the smallest, simplest shape in Gridhaven: a little box on little feet with a single glowing square on top. Everything is squared-off and deliberate like the city, but the heavy rounding, soft gaps and oversized face screen make it read as gentle and harmless, and its small careful hands and wide flat feet say it moves slowly and steps where it means to. The big two-eye screen does all the acting, sweeping left and right for its 'Check... no harm. Go.', while the cube antenna tip shifts from soft green certainty to amber checking. Faded, scuffed cream paint wearing to metal and a dull brass First Workshop stamp, ear discs and carry handle make it feel old, well made and once owned and loved, a warm note against the cool steel blue and safety yellow city and a natural friend to the greens and browns of the Old Grove."
}